AliasNull base userspace - versioned foundation artifact.

This is the first real, versioned AliasNull base-userspace artifact (Part 27-R,
extended by Part 27-S2). It is NOT a Linux filesystem, a rootfs image, a shell,
a package manager, or a set of system tools. It is a minimal, honest,
self-identifying foundation that AliasNull installs into its private runtime
directory and verifies before the runtime reports ready.

Since Part 27-S2 the artifact contains ONE real, source-built arm64 executable,
aliasnull_base_probe: the first genuine executable component of the AliasNull
base userspace. It is a small Android AArch64 PIE built from this repository
(app/src/main/cpp/aliasnull_base_probe.cpp) with the Android NDK, bundled as an
APK asset, and verified (SHA-256, 64-bit AArch64 ELF, executable permission)
before the runtime reports ready. It prints "AliasNull base userspace OK" and
exits 0. It is NOT a shell, NOT a general command runner, and NOT a Linux
userspace: AliasNull does not yet include Python, Git, a package manager, or
arbitrary command execution, and unknown Shell commands stay unknown. The
executable is exercised only through the controlled developer-diagnostic native
runtime test panel, never through the Shell command surface.

Contents of this artifact:
  VERSION              - the base artifact version (single source of truth)
  ARCH                 - the target architecture this build is produced for
  DESCRIPTION          - this description
  PROVENANCE.txt       - provenance and scope of every file in the artifact
  LICENSE.txt          - licensing note for the artifact files
  aliasnull_base_probe - the bundled 64-bit AArch64 base-userspace executable

Version:   see VERSION
Arch:      see ARCH
Produced:  from the AliasNull repository and shipped inside the signed APK. The
           executable is built from committed source by CI with the Android NDK
           (see PROVENANCE.txt); its expected SHA-256 is recorded in the
           base-userspace artifact manifest and is not silently hard-coded.
